WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:07.360
On February 22, 2022, a car crash in Chicago
escalated when one of the two drivers pulled

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:12.320
a gun and shot the other one in the leg.

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:17.240
While we don’t know much about the suspect,
we can assume that she had, at that instant,

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:25.510
limited capacity for sympathy, self-awareness,
empathy, meta-cognition and theory of mind.

00:00:25.510 --> 00:00:33.489
In short, she could have lacked social intelligence
and misinterpreted the incident as a deliberate

00:00:33.489 --> 00:00:39.770
attack.

00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:45.400
Social intelligence is the capacity to know
oneself and to know others — sometimes referred

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:51.510
to as "tact", "common sense", or "street smarts".

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:56.789
It's an innate human trait of neurotypical
minds, that gets refined through experience

00:00:56.789 --> 00:01:02.379
with people, and learning from success and
failure in social settings.

00:01:02.379 --> 00:01:07.939
Five distinct cognitive skills are at its
core.

00:01:07.939 --> 00:01:11.110
Sympathy is our tendency to feel with others.

00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:14.450
Parents naturally sympathize with their child.

00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:20.340
And babies experience stress when their mothers
are sad.

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:26.140
As we grow up, most of us show a lot of sympathy
for our family, some for our close circle

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:32.080
of friends and less for strangers.

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:37.079
Self-awareness is the ability to understand
our feelings.Toddlers that indicate they are

00:01:37.079 --> 00:01:39.610
hungry display that capacity.

00:01:39.610 --> 00:01:44.400
If they throw tantrums, it’s often because
they don’t understand their emotions.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:51.220
Although some are explicitly told not to express
what they feel.

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:54.520
As we get older we gain better self-awareness.

00:01:54.520 --> 00:02:01.840
Some people remain confused by their feelings
because they have learned to suppress them.

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:05.829
Empathy is our ability to understand what
others are feeling.

00:02:05.829 --> 00:02:09.920
Some children begin to show empathy as early
as kindergarten.

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:15.660
Others seem to lack this ability even when
they are far older.

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:19.990
Through years of social experiences we can
refine our empathy.

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:25.220
But those who never quite learned to understand
their own emotions, may also never learn to

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:30.420
sense the feelings of others.

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:34.420
Metacognition is an awareness of one's own
thought processes.

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:40.330
At age 4 most children display the first forms
of metacognitive skills when they begin to

00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:43.220
show what they know and what they don't know.

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:50.470
Soon after they learn to assess their level
of confidence in their own knowledge.

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:55.659
As adults, many of us get to know our brain
and learn that one of its jobs is to bring

00:02:55.659 --> 00:02:59.890
order to an inherently chaotic world of fact
and fiction.

00:02:59.890 --> 00:03:05.920
Some, however, get trapped in the stories
and lies they tell themselves to be true.

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:10.550
They don’t see that their minds can get
stuck in a web of biases.

00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:17.560
They remain unaware that they may be wrong
about certain assumptions.

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:23.420
Theory of mind is our ability to understand
what others know and how they think.

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:27.800
Children start to demonstrate theory of mind
around the age of 6.

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:32.870
They then realize that others may have different
information, and as a result draw different

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:34.440
conclusions.

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:38.840
This often leads to more empathy.

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:44.580
As adults, theory of mind allows us to understand
another person's perspective and their pattern

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:45.750
of thought.

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:51.640
Which makes it a powerful skill for influencing
others.

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:57.950
So sympathy, and self-awareness help us to
understand our emotions and meta-cognition

00:03:57.950 --> 00:03:59.280
our thoughts.

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:03.049
They provide us with knowledge about ourselves.

00:04:03.049 --> 00:04:08.760
Empathy allows us to appreciate what others
feel and theory of mind what goes on in their

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:14.430
heads: they allow us to understand others.

00:04:14.430 --> 00:04:19.090
Social intelligence is always formed within
a particular culture, which means we might

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:22.810
be clueless when put into a new social setting.

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:28.910
So while all 5 aspects are universally present,
they need to be refined for each particular

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:30.640
society.

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:35.590
Animals, by the way, show sympathy and empathy.

00:04:35.590 --> 00:04:39.330
Chimps even show a rudimentary ability for
theory of mind.

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:47.110
Humans, however, are the most socially intelligent
of all species.

00:04:47.110 --> 00:04:48.110
What do you think?

00:04:48.110 --> 00:04:53.440
Where does our high social intelligence come
from and how could we develop the five traits

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:57.190
further to increase our understanding of each
other?

00:04:57.190 --> 00:05:24.110
Share your thoughts in the 

00:05:24.110 --> 00:05:26.580
comments below.

